 "narrative": "All estimates and intervals are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. The formal feature_002-by-feature_037 interaction H102 is near null (R79: signed +0.023, interval -0.121 to +0.167), so meaningful amplification of the feature_002 association by feature_037=1 is not supported. The log_pfs_months interaction battery also does not support robust effect modification. H103 is close to but below threshold and crosses null (R80: +0.136, interval -0.013 to +0.286). H104 is opposite-signed and interval-crossing for feature_010 in the upper quartile (R81: -0.175, interval -0.420 to +0.070). H105 is essentially null for feature_037 in the upper quartile (R82: -0.003, interval -0.155 to +0.149). H107 and H108 are below threshold and interval-crossing in the lower quartile (R84: +0.112, interval -0.099 to +0.322; R85: -0.099, interval -0.259 to +0.061). H106 is a statistically opposite-signed interaction for feature_002 in the lower quartile (R83: -0.176, interval -0.334 to -0.018); however, the reverse-direction lower bound would be only +0.018, the pattern is similar to the previously failed H88 interaction, and this is one of many interaction tests, so I reject the registered positive interaction and do not register it as a meaningful reversed effect. The dominant-marker conditional checks are strong. Within feature_046 level_001, feature_002=1 remains associated with higher outcome_001 (R86: +0.855, interval +0.771 to +0.940), and feature_037=1 remains associated with lower outcome_001 (R87: +0.830, interval +0.748 to +0.911); I accept and close both as dataset-specific conditional robustness results. H101 feature_046 level_002 versus level_003 is small and interval-crossing (R88: +0.053, interval -0.098 to +0.204), so reject. H100 feature_050 is null/subthreshold (R90: +0.007, interval -0.114 to +0.127), so there is no reason to follow up the duplicate-looking feature_027. H99 was registered for a positive feature_063=1 versus 0 contrast, but R89 is signed negative (-0.227, interval -0.323 to -0.131), meaning the raw contrast is negative by about 0.23 units. Thus the registered positive claim is rejected, but the opposite sign is a potentially meaningful new lead and is registered as a reversed proposal. I request validation on H99 to independently check the raw feature_063 association because it is a new predictor after broad screening and could be a multiplicity artifact; if validation confirms a negative raw contrast with adequate precision, the reversed claim may be accepted, but the original positive claim should remain rejected. These conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
 "research_notes": "Updated plan. Dataset-specific core associations: feature_037=1 -> lower outcome_001 by roughly 0.75-0.83 units; feature_002=1 -> higher outcome_001 by roughly 0.78-0.99 units; feature_010=1 -> higher outcome_001 by roughly 0.31-0.58 units. Conditional robustness accepted across feature_037, feature_002, feature_010, feature_058, feature_038/018 halves, selected log_pfs_months quartiles, and feature_046 level_001. Interaction claims are generally null or subthreshold: feature_010-by-feature_037, feature_010-by-feature_002 after validation, feature_002-by-feature_037, and the log_pfs_months quartile battery are rejected/closed. H106 lower-quartile feature_002 interaction is opposite-sign significant but reversed lower bound only +0.018 and prior similar interaction failed validation, so no reversal. New lead: feature_063=1 raw negative by -0.227 (R89); H99 positive original is rejected, reversed claim registered unresolved. Validation requested on H99 to test raw feature_063 association. If validation confirms negative raw contrast and supports threshold, accept reversed claim; if null or uncertain, close. Feature_050 null, so deprioritize feature_027 duplicate check. Feature_046 marginal and level_002-vs-level_003 contrasts are subthreshold, so deprioritize further feature_046 main comparisons. Remaining broad binary screens H91-H98 stay active but lower priority; use future capacity if available. Avoid causal/mechanistic language and distinguish dataset-specific associations from generalizable claims.",
